window.HASHOP_CONSOLE_GUIDE = {"source":"D:\\fcj-workshop-haidang\\content\\5-Workshop","chapters":4,"steps":24,"images":46,"html":"\n<nav class=\"technical-toc reproduction-toc console-guide-toc\" aria-label=\"AWS Console workshop sections\"><a href=\"#hashop-console-prerequisites\"><span>01</span><span>Prerequisites</span></a><a href=\"#hashop-console-deployment\"><span>02</span><span>Deployment guide</span></a><a href=\"#hashop-console-validation\"><span>03</span><span>Test & validation</span></a><a href=\"#hashop-console-cleanup\"><span>05</span><span>Clean-up</span></a></nav>\n\n  <section class=\"technical-section console-guide-chapter\" id=\"hashop-console-prerequisites\">\n    <div class=\"technical-heading console-guide-chapter-heading\">\n      <p class=\"section-label\">01 — <span>Prerequisites</span></p>\n      <h2>Prerequisites</h2>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-intro\"><p>Before deploying HaShop, prepare the AWS account, target regions, and local tools below. These prerequisites reduce permission issues and make the deployment steps easier to reproduce.</p></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"console-guide-steps\">\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-3-1\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.3.1</span>\n        <h3>AWS account and permissions</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-3-1\" aria-label=\"Link to AWS account and permissions\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>The deployment requires an AWS account that can create and manage the main services used by HaShop:</p><ul><li>AWS CloudFormation</li><li>AWS WAF</li><li>Amazon S3</li><li>Amazon CloudFront</li><li>Amazon ECR</li><li>Amazon ECS Fargate</li><li>Application Load Balancer</li><li>Amazon VPC</li><li>Amazon RDS MySQL</li><li>Amazon Cognito</li><li>AWS Lambda</li><li>Amazon SNS</li><li>Amazon SQS</li><li>Amazon SES</li><li>AWS Secrets Manager</li><li>Amazon CloudWatch Logs</li><li>IAM Role and IAM Policy</li></ul><p>For a lab environment, <code>AdministratorAccess</code> can be used to avoid permission errors while practicing. For a real environment, create IAM roles and policies based on the principle of least privilege.</p></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-3-2\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.3.2</span>\n        <h3>Deployment regions</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-3-2\" aria-label=\"Link to Deployment regions\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>HaShop uses two AWS regions:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Region</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>us-east-1</code></td><td>Create the AWS WAF Web ACL for Amazon CloudFront.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ap-southeast-1</code></td><td>Deploy the main infrastructure of the system.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>When AWS WAF is associated with CloudFront, the Web ACL must use the <code>CLOUDFRONT</code> scope and must be created in <code>us-east-1</code>.</p></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-3-3\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.3.3</span>\n        <h3>Local tools</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-3-3\" aria-label=\"Link to Local tools\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Install the following tools on the deployment machine:</p><ul><li>Git</li><li>Node.js and npm</li><li>Docker Desktop</li><li>AWS CLI v2</li><li>PowerShell</li></ul><p>After installation, verify that the command line can access AWS:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws sts get-caller-identity\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The command should return the current AWS account ID, user or role ARN, and user ID.</p></div>\n    </article>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"technical-section console-guide-chapter\" id=\"hashop-console-deployment\">\n    <div class=\"technical-heading console-guide-chapter-heading\">\n      <p class=\"section-label\">02 — <span>Deployment guide</span></p>\n      <h2>Deployment guide</h2>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-intro\"><p>This section provides the end-to-end deployment guide for HaShop. Each step is separated into its own page so the process is easier to follow and verify.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> Direct folder paths used in this guide, such as <code>mkdir D:\\HaShop-release</code>, <code>cd D:\\HaShop-release</code>, or <code>cd D:\\HaShop-release\\cognito-post-confirmation-db</code>, are examples for reference only. Replace them with the real path to the workspace folder on your own machine.</p></blockquote></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"console-guide-steps\">\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-1\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.1</span>\n        <h3>Create the Lambda artifact S3 bucket</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-1\" aria-label=\"Link to Create the Lambda artifact S3 bucket\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>First, create the <code>D:\\HaShop-release</code> folder. This folder will be used as the main release workspace for the whole HaShop deployment, including storing project source files, Lambda packages, CloudFormation templates, and other artifacts needed throughout the deployment guide. After creating the workspace, clone the Lambda PostConfirmation repository into it.</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>mkdir D:\\HaShop-release\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>cd D:\\HaShop-release\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>git clone https<span style=color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010>:</span>//github.com/Leviethaidang/cognito-post-confirmation-db.git\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Set the deployment variables:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$REGION = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;ap-southeast-1&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ACCOUNT_ID = $(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ARTIFACT_BUCKET = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop-artifacts-</span>$ACCOUNT_ID<span style=color:#e6db74>-</span>$REGION<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Create the artifact bucket:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3api create-bucket `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --bucket $ARTIFACT_BUCKET `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --region $REGION `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Enable Block Public Access:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3api put-public-access-block `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --bucket $ARTIFACT_BUCKET `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --public-access-block-configuration BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Enable server-side encryption:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$SSE_CONFIG = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>$env:TEMP<span style=color:#e6db74>\\hashop-s3-sse.json&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span><span style=color:#e6db74>@&#39;\n</span></span></span><span style=display:flex><span><span style=color:#e6db74>{&#34;Rules&#34;: [{&#34;ApplyServerSideEncryptionByDefault&#34;: {&#34;SSEAlgorithm&#34;: &#34;AES256&#34;}}]}\n</span></span></span><span style=display:flex><span><span style=color:#e6db74>&#39;@</span> | Set-Content -Path $SSE_CONFIG -Encoding ascii\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3api put-bucket-encryption `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --bucket $ARTIFACT_BUCKET `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --server-side-encryption-configuration <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;file://</span>$SSE_CONFIG<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image1.png\" alt=\"Create Lambda artifact bucket\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Create Lambda artifact bucket</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-2\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.2</span>\n        <h3>Package and upload Lambda PostConfirmation</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-2\" aria-label=\"Link to Package and upload Lambda PostConfirmation\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Lambda PostConfirmation is invoked by Amazon Cognito after a user confirms an account. This function stores user information in Amazon RDS MySQL.</p><p>Keep using the same terminal window from the previous step and run the following commands there. This terminal session already contains the deployment variables:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$REGION = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;ap-southeast-1&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ACCOUNT_ID = $(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ARTIFACT_BUCKET = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop-artifacts-</span>$ACCOUNT_ID<span style=color:#e6db74>-</span>$REGION<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Move to the Lambda source folder:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>cd D:\\HaShop-release\\cognito-post-confirmation-db\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Install the required dependency:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>npm install mysql2\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Compress the source code into <code>function.zip</code>:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>Compress-Archive `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  -Path .\\index.js, .\\node_modules, .\\package.json, .\\package-lock.json `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  -DestinationPath .\\function.zip `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  -Force\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Upload the package to the artifact bucket:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3 cp .\\function.zip <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;s3://</span>$ARTIFACT_BUCKET<span style=color:#e6db74>/lambda/post-confirmation/function.zip&#34;</span> --region $REGION\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Verify that the file exists:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3 ls <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;s3://</span>$ARTIFACT_BUCKET<span style=color:#e6db74>/lambda/post-confirmation/function.zip&#34;</span> --region $REGION\n</span></span></code></pre></div><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image2.png\" alt=\"Upload Lambda PostConfirmation package\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Upload Lambda PostConfirmation package</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-3\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.3</span>\n        <h3>Create ECR repositories and push Docker images</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-3\" aria-label=\"Link to Create ECR repositories and push Docker images\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Set variables for the target AWS account and ECR registry:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$REGION = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;ap-southeast-1&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ACCOUNT_ID = $(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$ECR = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>$ACCOUNT_ID<span style=color:#e6db74>.dkr.ecr.</span>$REGION<span style=color:#e6db74>.amazonaws.com&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Create the ECR repositories used by the microservices:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$REPOS = @(\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/user-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/product-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/inventory-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/cart-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/order-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/payment-service&#34;</span>,\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/notification-service&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>)\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span><span style=color:#66d9ef>foreach</span> ($repo <span style=color:#66d9ef>in</span> $REPOS) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  aws ecr describe-repositories --repository-names $repo --region $REGION *&gt; $null\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#66d9ef>if</span> ($LASTEXITCODE <span style=color:#f92672>-ne</span> <span style=color:#ae81ff>0</span>) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>    aws ecr create-repository `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>      --repository-name $repo `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>      --image-scanning-configuration scanOnPush=true `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>      --region $REGION\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  }\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>}\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Log in Docker to Amazon ECR:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws ecr get-login-password --region $REGION | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin $ECR\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>If the terminal shows <code>Login Succeeded</code>, Docker can push images to ECR.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image3.png\" alt=\"Docker login to ECR\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Docker login to ECR</figcaption></figure><p>Download the tested container image release package:</p><p><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1o9IrPV95KHFCW1tLL5gyHjRJ-FIiyEql/view?usp=drive_link\">HaShop Docker images package</a></p><p>Extract the package into <code>D:\\HaShop-release\\HaShop-docker-images</code>, then run:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$IMAGE_DIR = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;D:\\HaShop-release\\HaShop-docker-images&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$IMAGES = @(\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/user-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;user-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/product-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;product-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/inventory-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;inventory-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/cart-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;cart-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/order-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;order-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/payment-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;payment-service.tar&#34;</span>},\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  @{Repo=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;hashop/notification-service&#34;</span>; File=<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;notification-service.tar&#34;</span>}\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>)\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span><span style=color:#66d9ef>foreach</span> ($img <span style=color:#66d9ef>in</span> $IMAGES) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  $tarPath = Join-Path $IMAGE_DIR $img.File\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  $loadOutput = docker load -i $tarPath\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  $sourceImage = $null\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#66d9ef>foreach</span> ($line <span style=color:#66d9ef>in</span> $loadOutput) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>    <span style=color:#66d9ef>if</span> ($line <span style=color:#f92672>-match</span> <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;Loaded image:\\s*(.+)$&#34;</span>) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>      $sourceImage = $Matches[<span style=color:#ae81ff>1</span>].Trim()\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>    }\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  }\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  <span style=color:#66d9ef>if</span> (<span style=color:#f92672>-not</span> $sourceImage) {\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>    Write-Host <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;Cannot detect the image name after docker load. Run docker images to check.&#34;</span> -ForegroundColor Red\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>    <span style=color:#66d9ef>break</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  }\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  $targetImage = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span>$ECR<span style=color:#e6db74>/</span>$($img.Repo)<span style=color:#e6db74>:latest&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  docker tag $sourceImage $targetImage\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  docker push $targetImage\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>}\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>If the image package is stored in another folder, update <code>$IMAGE_DIR</code> to the actual path.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image4.png\" alt=\"Load and push Docker images\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Load and push Docker images</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image5.png\" alt=\"Docker images pushed to ECR\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Docker images pushed to ECR</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-4\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.4</span>\n        <h3>Clone the CloudFormation repository</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-4\" aria-label=\"Link to Clone the CloudFormation repository\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Return to the release folder and clone the CloudFormation templates:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>cd D:\\HaShop-release\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>git clone https<span style=color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010>:</span>//github.com/Leviethaidang/cloudformation.git\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The repository contains the templates used in the next step:</p><ul><li><code>00-cf-hashop-global-waf.yaml</code></li><li><code>01-cf-hashop-foundation.yaml</code></li><li><code>02-cf-hashop-ecs-services.yaml</code></li><li><code>03-cf-hashop-db-init.yaml</code></li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image6.png\" alt=\"Clone CloudFormation repository\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Clone CloudFormation repository</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-5\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.5</span>\n        <h3>Deploy CloudFormation stacks</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-5\" aria-label=\"Link to Deploy CloudFormation stacks\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><h2 id=stack-0-global-waf>Stack 0: Global WAF</h2><p>Switch the AWS Console region to <strong>United States (N. Virginia) <code>us-east-1</code></strong>. Open CloudFormation and create a stack with an existing template. Upload <code>00-cf-hashop-global-waf.yaml</code>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image7.png\" alt=\"Upload WAF template\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Upload WAF template</figcaption></figure><p>Choose <strong>Next</strong>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image8.png\" alt=\"CloudFormation WAF stack details\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>CloudFormation WAF stack details</figcaption></figure><p>Set the stack name to <code>HaShop-WAF</code>, then continue with <strong>Next</strong>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image9.png\" alt=\"Set WAF stack name\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Set WAF stack name</figcaption></figure><p>Review the configuration and choose <strong>Submit</strong>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image10.png\" alt=\"Submit WAF stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Submit WAF stack</figcaption></figure><p>After the stack is created, open the <strong>Outputs</strong> tab and copy <code>FrontendWebAclArn</code>. This ARN will be used when deploying the foundation stack.</p><h2 id=stack-01-foundation>Stack 01: Foundation</h2><p>Switch the AWS Console region back to <strong>Singapore <code>ap-southeast-1</code></strong>. Create another CloudFormation stack and upload <code>01-cf-hashop-foundation.yaml</code>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image11.png\" alt=\"Upload foundation template\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Upload foundation template</figcaption></figure><p>Set the stack name exactly to <code>cf-hashop-foundation</code>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image12.png\" alt=\"Set foundation stack name\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Set foundation stack name</figcaption></figure><p>Provide the required parameters:</p><ul><li><code>DbPassword</code>: choose a database password.</li><li><code>InternalApiKey</code>: choose a 16-character internal API key.</li><li><code>AdminEmail</code>: enter your email address.</li><li><code>SesFromEmail</code>: enter the SES verified sender email address.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image13.png\" alt=\"Foundation stack parameters\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Foundation stack parameters</figcaption></figure><p>Set the Lambda artifact parameters:</p><ul><li><code>LambdaCodeS3Bucket</code>: <code>hashop-artifacts-&lt;ACCOUNT_ID>-ap-southeast-1</code></li><li><code>LambdaCodeS3Key</code>: <code>lambda/post-confirmation/function.zip</code></li><li><code>FrontendWebAclArn</code>: the ARN copied from Stack 0</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image14.png\" alt=\"Foundation Lambda and WAF parameters\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Foundation Lambda and WAF parameters</figcaption></figure><p>Continue to the review page, acknowledge that CloudFormation may create IAM resources with custom names, and submit the stack.</p><p>If ECS tasks fail because IAM roles have not propagated yet, delete the failed stack and run it again.</p><h2 id=stack-02-ecs-services>Stack 02: ECS services</h2><p>Wait until Stack 01 finishes. It can take around 20 minutes. Then create a new CloudFormation stack using <code>02-cf-hashop-ecs-services.yaml</code>. Set the stack name to <code>cf-hashop-ecs</code>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image15.png\" alt=\"Create ECS services stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Create ECS services stack</figcaption></figure><p>In the container image parameters, replace <code>&lt;ACCOUNT_ID></code> with the real AWS account ID.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image16.png\" alt=\"ECS container image parameters\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>ECS container image parameters</figcaption></figure><h2 id=stack-03-database-initialization>Stack 03: Database initialization</h2><p>Stack 03 can be started after Stack 02 is submitted. Create a new CloudFormation stack using <code>03-cf-hashop-db-init.yaml</code>.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image17.png\" alt=\"Upload database initialization template\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Upload database initialization template</figcaption></figure><p>Set a stack name for the database initialization stack.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image18.png\" alt=\"Database initialization stack name\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Database initialization stack name</figcaption></figure><p>Review the stack configuration.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image19.png\" alt=\"Database initialization review\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Database initialization review</figcaption></figure><p>Acknowledge that CloudFormation may create IAM resources with custom names, then submit the stack.</p></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-4-6\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.4.6</span>\n        <h3>Prepare and publish the frontend</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-4-6\" aria-label=\"Link to Prepare and publish the frontend\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Clone the frontend repository from the release folder:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>cd D:\\HaShop-release\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>git clone https<span style=color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010>:</span>//github.com/Leviethaidang/Front-end.git\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>cd Front-end\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Use the <code>main</code> branch because it is the stable version that has been tested for this deployment.</p><p>After Stack 01 is created successfully, open the stack outputs and copy:</p><ul><li><code>FrontendBucketName</code></li><li><code>FrontendCloudFrontDistributionId</code></li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image20.png\" alt=\"Frontend stack outputs\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Frontend stack outputs</figcaption></figure><p>Set the frontend deployment variables:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>$FRONTEND_BUCKET = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;&lt;FrontendBucketName&gt;&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$REGION = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;ap-southeast-1&#34;</span>\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>$FRONTEND_DISTRIBUTION_ID = <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;&lt;FrontendCloudFrontDistributionId&gt;&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Sync the frontend source to the S3 frontend bucket:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws s3 sync <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;.&#34;</span> <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;s3://</span>$FRONTEND_BUCKET<span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;</span> `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --delete `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --region $REGION\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Create a CloudFront invalidation so users receive the latest frontend files:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-powershell data-lang=powershell><span style=display:flex><span>aws cloudfront create-invalidation `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --distribution-id $FRONTEND_DISTRIBUTION_ID `\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>  --paths <span style=color:#e6db74>&#34;/*&#34;</span>\n</span></span></code></pre></div><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image21.png\" alt=\"Sync frontend to S3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Sync frontend to S3</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-deployment/image22.png\" alt=\"Create CloudFront invalidation\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Create CloudFront invalidation</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"technical-section console-guide-chapter\" id=\"hashop-console-validation\">\n    <div class=\"technical-heading console-guide-chapter-heading\">\n      <p class=\"section-label\">03 — <span>Test & validation</span></p>\n      <h2>Test & validation</h2>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-intro\"><p>After deployment, validate the system from the user interface, AWS Console, logs, and security monitoring views. The expected result is that the frontend is reachable, services are healthy, business flows work, and no critical runtime errors appear in logs.</p></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"console-guide-steps\">\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-1\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.1</span>\n        <h3>Access the frontend</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-1\" aria-label=\"Link to Access the frontend\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Open a browser and access the CloudFront domain:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-text data-lang=text><span style=display:flex><span>https://&lt;FrontendCloudFrontDomain&gt;\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p><code>&lt;FrontendCloudFrontDomain></code> is taken from the Outputs tab of the <code>cf-hashop-foundation</code> stack.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The HaShop home page loads successfully.</li><li>Static assets are served through CloudFront.</li><li>The page does not show a browser-side loading error.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image1.png\" alt=\"HaShop frontend loaded successfully\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>HaShop frontend loaded successfully</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-2\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.2</span>\n        <h3>Admin login and authorization</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-2\" aria-label=\"Link to Admin login and authorization\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Use the default admin account to sign in:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-text data-lang=text><span style=display:flex><span>Email: admin@example.com\n</span></span><span style=display:flex><span>Password: Letmein123!!!\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>After signing in, open the admin functions such as product management.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The admin account can sign in successfully.</li><li>Admin-only pages can be opened after authentication.</li><li>Requests that require authorization are sent with a valid token.</li><li>The user is not redirected back to the login page unexpectedly.</li></ul></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-3\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.3</span>\n        <h3>Check ECS services</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-3\" aria-label=\"Link to Check ECS services\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>In the AWS Console, open:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-text data-lang=text><span style=display:flex><span>Amazon ECS -&gt; Clusters -&gt; cf-hashop-test-cluster -&gt; Services\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li><code>user-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>product-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>inventory-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>cart-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>order-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>payment-api</code> is running.</li><li><code>payment-worker</code> is running.</li><li><code>order-worker</code> is running.</li><li><code>notification-worker</code> is running.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image2.png\" alt=\"ECS services running\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>ECS services running</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-4\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.4</span>\n        <h3>Add a product</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-4\" aria-label=\"Link to Add a product\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Sign in with the admin account and open product management.</p><p>Enter the basic product information:</p><ul><li>Product name</li><li>Description</li><li>Price</li><li>Main image</li><li>Additional images</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image3.png\" alt=\"Enter product information\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Enter product information</figcaption></figure><p>Add product variants and quantity for each variant.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image4.png\" alt=\"Add product variants and inventory\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Add product variants and inventory</figcaption></figure><p>Choose <strong>Create</strong> to create the product.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The product is created successfully.</li><li>The product appears on the home page or product listing page.</li><li>Product images and variant information are displayed correctly.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image5.png\" alt=\"Product appears in product list\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Product appears in product list</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image6.png\" alt=\"Product appears on HaShop frontend\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Product appears on HaShop frontend</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-5\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.5</span>\n        <h3>Customer registration, login, profile update, and payment method</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-5\" aria-label=\"Link to Customer registration, login, profile update, and payment method\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>This test validates the customer account flow on the HaShop frontend. The purpose is to confirm that a new customer can create an account, verify the account by email, sign in, update profile information, and add a payment method before continuing to the order flow.</p><h2 id=register-a-customer-account>Register a customer account</h2><p>Open the HaShop registration page and enter the required customer information, including full name, email address, phone number, password, and password confirmation.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image1.png\" alt=\"Customer registration page\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Customer registration page</figcaption></figure><p>After submitting the form, check the registered email inbox for the verification code. If the email does not appear in the inbox, check the spam or junk mail folder.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image2.png\" alt=\"Verification email\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Verification email</figcaption></figure><p>Enter the OTP code on the email verification page to activate the customer account.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image3.png\" alt=\"Email verification page\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Email verification page</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image4.png\" alt=\"Email verification completed\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Email verification completed</figcaption></figure><h2 id=log-in-with-the-customer-account>Log in with the customer account</h2><p>After the account is verified successfully, return to the login page and sign in with the newly created customer account.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image5.png\" alt=\"Customer login page\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Customer login page</figcaption></figure><h2 id=update-profile-and-payment-method>Update profile and payment method</h2><p>From the customer account area, open <code>Profile</code>, then choose the edit profile option.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image6.png\" alt=\"Customer profile page\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Customer profile page</figcaption></figure><p>Update the customer information, add the delivery address, and link MoMo as the payment method.</p><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/customer-account/image7.png\" alt=\"Edit profile and add payment method\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Edit profile and add payment method</figcaption></figure><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The customer account can be registered successfully.</li><li>The OTP verification email is received and can be used to verify the account.</li><li>The customer can log in after successful verification.</li><li>Profile information, address, and MoMo payment method can be saved successfully.</li></ul></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-6\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.6</span>\n        <h3>Validate the order flow</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-6\" aria-label=\"Link to Validate the order flow\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Run the following order scenarios on the website:</p><ol><li>Admin creates category, size, color, product, and inventory.</li><li>Customer adds a product to the cart.</li><li>Customer checks out with COD.</li><li>Customer checks out with the MOMO/BANK demo payment method.</li><li>Check the order status.</li></ol><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>COD orders are confirmed directly.</li><li>MOMO/BANK orders move to the pending payment state.</li><li><code>payment-worker</code> processes messages from SQS.</li><li><code>order-worker</code> updates order status after payment results are available.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image7.png\" alt=\"Order checkout flow\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Order checkout flow</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image8.png\" alt=\"Order status validation\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Order status validation</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-7\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.7</span>\n        <h3>Review CloudWatch logs</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-7\" aria-label=\"Link to Review CloudWatch logs\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>In the AWS Console, open:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-text data-lang=text><span style=display:flex><span>CloudWatch -&gt; Log groups\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Find the log groups for the ECS services and related Lambda function. Review logs for:</p><ul><li><code>user-api</code></li><li><code>product-api</code></li><li><code>inventory-api</code></li><li><code>cart-api</code></li><li><code>order-api</code></li><li><code>payment-api</code></li><li><code>payment-worker</code></li><li><code>order-worker</code></li><li><code>notification-worker</code></li><li>Lambda PostConfirmation</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image9.png\" alt=\"CloudWatch log groups\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>CloudWatch log groups</figcaption></figure><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>No critical errors such as <code>CannotPullContainerError</code>.</li><li>No database connection failure.</li><li>No JWT verification failure.</li><li>No SQS permission denied error.</li></ul></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-5-8\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.5.8</span>\n        <h3>Check AWS WAF</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-5-8\" aria-label=\"Link to Check AWS WAF\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>In the AWS Console, open:</p><div class=highlight><pre tabindex=0 style=color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none><code class=language-text data-lang=text><span style=display:flex><span>AWS WAF -&gt; Web ACLs -&gt; Global / CloudFront -&gt; HaShop Web ACL\n</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Check the following WAF views:</p><ul><li>Allowed requests</li><li>Blocked requests</li><li>Sampled requests</li><li>Rule metrics</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image10.png\" alt=\"AWS WAF metrics\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>AWS WAF metrics</figcaption></figure><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The WAF Web ACL is associated with CloudFront.</li><li>Request metrics are available.</li><li>Sampled requests can be inspected for validation.</li></ul></div>\n    </article>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n  <section class=\"technical-section console-guide-chapter\" id=\"hashop-console-cleanup\">\n    <div class=\"technical-heading console-guide-chapter-heading\">\n      <p class=\"section-label\">05 — <span>Clean-up</span></p>\n      <h2>Clean-up</h2>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-intro\"><p>Clean-up must be performed after the lab to avoid unnecessary AWS costs. Delete resources in the correct order because some stacks depend on resources created by earlier stacks.</p></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"console-guide-steps\">\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-1\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.1</span>\n        <h3>Delete the DB init stack</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-1\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete the DB init stack\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Delete the DB init stack first if it still exists.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image11.png\" alt=\"Delete the DB init stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete the DB init stack</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-2\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.2</span>\n        <h3>Delete the ECS services stack</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-2\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete the ECS services stack\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Delete the ECS services stack after the database initialization stack is removed.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image12.png\" alt=\"Delete the ECS services stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete the ECS services stack</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-3\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.3</span>\n        <h3>Empty S3 buckets created by the foundation stack</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-3\" aria-label=\"Link to Empty S3 buckets created by the foundation stack\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Before deleting the foundation stack, empty the S3 buckets created by the stack. CloudFormation cannot delete non-empty buckets automatically.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image13.png\" alt=\"Empty S3 buckets created by the foundation stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Empty S3 buckets created by the foundation stack</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-4\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.4</span>\n        <h3>Delete the foundation stack</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-4\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete the foundation stack\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Wait until Stack 02 and Stack 03 are fully deleted, then delete the foundation stack.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image14.png\" alt=\"Delete the foundation stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete the foundation stack</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-5\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.5</span>\n        <h3>Delete the WAF stack</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-5\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete the WAF stack\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Switch the AWS Console region to N. Virginia <code>us-east-1</code>, then delete the WAF stack.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image15.png\" alt=\"Delete the WAF stack\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete the WAF stack</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-6\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.6</span>\n        <h3>Delete ECR repositories</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-6\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete ECR repositories\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Open Amazon ECR, go to Private registry, then Repositories. Delete all HaShop repositories that were created for the lab.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image16.png\" alt=\"Delete ECR repositories\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete ECR repositories</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    <article class=\"console-guide-step\" id=\"hashop-console-5-7-7\">\n      <header class=\"console-guide-step-heading\">\n        <span>5.7.7</span>\n        <h3>Delete artifact and template buckets</h3>\n        <a href=\"#hashop-console-5-7-7\" aria-label=\"Link to Delete artifact and template buckets\">#</a>\n      </header>\n      <div class=\"console-guide-body\"><p>Delete the artifact bucket and any template buckets created automatically by CloudFormation.</p><p>Expected result:</p><ul><li>The target resource is deleted successfully.</li><li>No dependent stack remains in a failed deletion state.</li><li>The AWS account no longer keeps resources that can generate lab costs.</li></ul><figure class=\"console-guide-figure\"><img src=\"assets/projects/hashop/workshop/hashop-test-cleanup/image17.png\" alt=\"Delete artifact and template buckets\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption>Delete artifact and template buckets</figcaption></figure></div>\n    </article>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n<footer class=\"technical-footer reproduction-footer console-guide-footer\">\n  <div>\n    <p class=\"section-label\">Workshop source</p>\n    <h2>AWS Console deployment, validation and clean-up</h2>\n    <p>This view reproduces the practical English workshop content from sections 5.3–5.5 and 5.7, including the original screenshots and local preparation commands.</p>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"technical-actions\">\n    <a class=\"technical-action technical-action--primary\" href=\"https://github.com/Leviethaidang/cloudformation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Open CloudFormation</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></a>\n    <a class=\"technical-action\" href=\"HighlightedProjects/HaShop/TechnicalDeepDive/\"><span>Back to technical deep dive</span><span aria-hidden=\"true\">←</span></a>\n  </div>\n</footer>"};
